\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico Stocks Close Dn 0.4% Despite Late Rally \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1995\par 22:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexican stocks closed lower Friday, despite a late surge of buying interest in the final hour of trading ahead of a three-day holiday weekend. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the overall mood was apathetic in the final session of 1995, with most market players waiting for January to arrive before making new moves. \par \par \uc2  According to preliminary official information, the market's key IPC index closed down 12.29 points to 2,778.47 - a drop of 0.4%. At the end of 1994, the IPC stood at 2,375.66. \par \par \uc2  Volume totaled 871.1 million pesos on 110.9 million shares traded. \par \par \uc2  'Except for a bit of a year-end push at the end, there was a lack of interest in the market today,' said one local trader. 'Anybody who really wanted to sell today had to pay a price for it.' \par \par \uc2  The IPC sank to an intraday low of 2,747.28, 1.6% below Thursday's close, around 2010 GMT before some speculative buys surfaced in the final 50 minutes of trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said most financial institutions had already shut down for the day in early afternoon trading, though, with most foreign players getting out early. \par \par \uc2  Another less-than-stellar performance in the peso helped dampen investor spirits, according to traders. As reported, the spot dollar ended the day almost flat at around 7.70 pesos, but only after \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The spot dollar had moved as high as 7.74 pesos in intraday trading, after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell 1.0% Thursday to sink to a 10-day low. \par \par \uc2  Mexican financial markets will be closed Monday for the New Year's Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-12-95 \par \par \uc2  2137GMT \par \par \uc2  5047 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drct0aahj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
