\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico Stocks Open Dn 0.4% Ahead Of Long Weekend \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 1995\par 16:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexican stocks opened slightly lower in light volume Friday as market players shuffled positionson the final trading day of 1995 in the wake of recent peso declines. \par \par \uc2  Around 1500 GMT, the market's key IPC index was off 10.41 points to 2,780.35 - a drop of 0.4%. At the end of 1994, the IPC stood at 2,375.66. \par \par \uc2  Volume totaled 14.7 million pesos on 1.4 million shares traded. \par \par \uc2  An early drop in bellwether Telefonos de Mexico (Telmex), the national telephone monopoly, was hurting the overall market. Telmex 'L' series shares - those available to foreign investors - were off 14 centavos, or 1.1%, to 12.36 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Telmex shares have declined this week despite government approval on substantial long distance rate hikes effective Jan. 1. \par \par \uc2  'I think what we've seen this week is people shuffling their positions before the end of the year, rather than any reaction to news,' said a local trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders added there was some continued concern about the recent performance of the peso, which declined 1.0% against the dollar Thursday to land at a 10-day low. Still, others speculated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if new pressures surfaced Friday ahead of a three-day weekend. \par \par \uc2  'Overall, it should be a very quiet day ahead of the holiday,' said a local stock dealer, adding that a lot of market players had already closed up shop for 1995. \par \par \uc2  The IPC has dropped four straight sessions, after surging 3.2% Dec. 21 to end at a 15-month high. Financial markets will be closed Monday for New Year's Day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-12-95 \par \par \uc2  1501GMT \par \par \uc2  5047 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drct0a9gn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
