\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Cetes break downward trend in auction. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robert Kozak \par \uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Dec 11 (Reuter) - Mexico's Cetes, or treasury bills, broke the downward trend in rates in this week's primary auction because last week's sharp decline was met by pressure on the exchange rate, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The rate on bellwether 28-day Cetes rose 205 basis points to 50.31 percent, while the 91-day Cetes rate rose 128 basis points to 49.73 percent and the 182-day rate rose 82 basis points to 47.73 percent, Banco de Mexico said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said they had expected the 28-day rate to rise about 200 basis points above last week's 48.26 percent. They based their expectations on the 190 basis point rise in secondary Cetes rates and in auctions to add liquidity to the market. Same-day Cetes rates closed on Monday at 51.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts had worried that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to knock down rates too far and too fast after last week's sharp 520 basis point decline in the 28-day paper. \par \par \uc2  "Pressure on the exchange rate was behind this rebound in the interest rates," one market specialist said. \par \par \uc2  In the last few days of trading last, the Mexican peso fell to below 7.80 pesos per dollar -- a key psychological barrier. \par \par \uc2  The Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets late on Friday to boost the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The peso was also under pressure from year-end demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  The rates on the 28-day paper had fallen steadily since November 14, when they reached 59.99 percent at the auction. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the rebound in the Cetes rates was probably also due to 48 percent being considered a floor for primary rates, since inflation for December is seen coming in at about four percent for the month, leaving the possibility of negative real rates. \par \par \uc2  The Banco de Mexico assigned 1.10 billon pesos offered at 28 and 91 days and 700 millon at 182 days. \par \par \uc2  The auction took place one day earlier than normal because of a religious holiday in Mexico on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289500 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drcc00s61\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
