\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 /Ortiz/Growth -4:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 1995\par 00:35\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Finance Minsiter Ortiz's GDP growth forecast of 3% incorporated a series of economic assumptions. These are a primary fiscal surplus of 4% of GDP; inflation of 20.5% annualized; and a current account deficit of 1% of GDP. \par \par \uc2  Ortiz said the government monetary program for next year incorporates a floating exchange rate, market determined interest rates, and sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market whenever imbalances appear. \par \par \uc2  "We will not defend any type of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band or a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level," Ortiz said. He added, however, that the government budget incorporates an exchange rate of 7.70 peso to the dollar. The peso ended the day at 7.7350 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Ortiz called the government's 1996 budget "sound, realistic and sustainable." \par \par \uc2  He noted that the budget is based on an oil price of $13.25 per barrel, despite private sector forcasts for higher oil prices in 1996. Ortiz added the budget does not include proceeds from any privatization. \par \par \uc2  --Terence Donnelly \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 12-12-95 \par \par \uc2  1835EST \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011025drcc00d08\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
