\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's 24,48-hr pesos close lower in dull trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Dec 11 (Reuter) - Mexico's peso, slumbering through a slack trading session before Tuesday's national holiday, ended slightly lower, with traders reporting marginal dollar demand because of the approaching year-end. \par \par \uc2  The widely watched 48-hour peso closed off three centavos at 7.745/7.760 pesos per dollar, while the 24-hour contract shadowed its counterpart to end at 7.730/7.750 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The market continues a little under pressure because of year-end, but it is nothing to worry about because there is very low volume," one trader said, adding that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  seem to have calmed speculator activity. \par \par \uc2  The Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in selling dollars on Friday to stem a run on the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was the third time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last month. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the expected increase in rates at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly primary auction later Monday could put more pressure on the peso in coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  Rates are seen edging higher, not least because of tradition inflationary pressures in December, Mexico's peak month for consumer price increases. \par \par \uc2  Same-day pesos closed unchanged at 7.710/7.730 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  --Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289562 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drcb00z1h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
