\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso -2: Trading Volume Could Stay Low \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1995\par 21:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said a lot of Mexican investment funds had already closed out the year, a factor that could spell continued low trading volume in the final weeks of 1995. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed 0.7% weaker against the dollar Friday, despite some late \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As reported, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, pushing the spot dollar down about five centavos toward the end of trading. Dealers speculated the amount involved was $50 million or even less, with overall trading volume very low. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso Nov. 9 and Nov. 14. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said they will stick to a free-floating exchange policy, but that they reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a discretionary manner on occasion. \par \par \uc2  In other news, the finance ministry said Friday Mexico booked an $837-million trade surplus in October. It reported Thursday industrial production fell 8.0% in the first nine months of 1995 compared with the year-earlier period. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, reported consumer prices rose 2.5% in November, up from 2.1% in October. Some economists have predicted monthly inflation will hit 4% in December, due to seasonal factors and a hike in gas prices. \par \par \uc2  The peso ended Monday down 55% against the dollar since Dec. 20, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-12-95 \par \par \uc2  2015GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drcb09vf0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
