\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's peso down slightly after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Dec 8 (Reuter) - The Mexican peso closed marginally lower after Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the 24-hour unit hit a minimum of 7.80/7.82 and the 48-hour 7.72/7.84 to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost up to 12 centavos against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But at the close the 24-hour peso finished at 7.70/7.72, and the 48-hour one -- considered the spot -- was at 7.71/7.73, representing slight falls of 2.0 centavos and 1.0 centavo against the dollar, respectively. \par \par \uc2  "Once again, we have seen that the Banco de Mexico is not going to let the market go over 7.80 pesos and we also saw that they are following a strategy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  a little before the close of the market," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly, we are going to see that many are going to end the week with loses," the dealer added, making reference to several market players who were speculating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it was selling dollars to support the peso, but did not specify the amount. Dealers speculated it could have been about $100 million. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drc800wt9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal33