\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's Peso Closes Weaker Vs Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1995\par 21:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY (AP-DJ)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso closed weaker in thin trading against the dollar Friday, despite some late \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex quoted the dollar closing at a mid rate level of 7.7350 pesos against 7.6850 pesos at Thursday's close. Spreads were 7.7100/7.7600 pesos per dollar, compared with 7.6600/7.7100 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market suffered under a slight liquidity crunch Friday, with few dollars entering the market and some typical end-of-year dollar demand by corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  Exacerbating the peso's weakness was the weekend and next Tuesday's holiday. Local financial markets will be closed Tuesday for a national religious holiday, meaning 48-hour contracts will be tied up until Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  After opening weaker at 7.7350/dlr, the peso slowly eased to a mid rate at 7.8150 pesos by 1830 GMT, then moved to around 7.7850 pesos before the spot dollar suddenly dropped in the final 30 minutes of trading. \par \par \uc2  As reported, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesperson confirmed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. The spokesperson could not provide the amount involved. \par \par \uc2  The sudden appearance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last half hour of trading surprised dealers. Minutes before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers were confident that the bank would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  'Weeks ago, the volatility was being caused by speculation,' said a dealer shortly before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 'Now the volatility is being caused by the typical needs of domestic corporations.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-12-95 \par \par \uc2  2010GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drc809rlw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
