\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes -2: Peso Advances 0.5% Vs. Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 1995\par 21:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Secondary money market rates continued to drop Thursday after they closed Wednesday at 53.55%. \par \par \uc2  Bellwether 28-day primary Cetes rates fell 5.25 percentage points to 54.74% at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly Treasury bill auction Tuesday - the first primary rate decline in nine weeks. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Mexico reported Wednesday that the average interbank lending rate (TIIP) stood at 55.3731%, down 14.3415% from the previous week. \par \par \uc2  Though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported lower international reserves late Wednesday, dealers said the decline was in line with their expectations. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said international reserves in dollar terms stood at $13.746 billion as of November 17, down $317 million from $14.063 billion as of November 10. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported it spent $125 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the one-week period. As reported, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed last week that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market November 14. \par \par \uc2  According to Banamex's quotations, the peso closed 0.5% stronger against the dollar from Wednesday's close, and is down 55% against the dollar since Dec. 20, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  The peso has gained on the dollar in four of the last five trading sessions after it sank to a historic closing low of 7.9100 to the dollar November 15. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar ended September at 6.3850 pesos and closed October at 7.0650 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Trading of peso futures on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange was closed for the Thanksgiving holiday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2053GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbn09f7e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
