\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens -3: Intl Reserves Dn $317 Mln \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 1995\par 16:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City a little before 1550 GMT, on spot dollar markets, the dollar was trading at mid rate levels of 7.6350 pesos. \par \par \uc2  The peso gained 1.1% on the dollar Wednesday. It strengthened against the dollar in three of the last four trading sessions, after sinking to a historic closing low of 7.9100 pesos November 15. \par \par \uc2  Though the Bank of Mexico reported lower international reserves, dealers said the decline was in line with their expectations. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said international reserves in dollar terms stood at $13.746 billion as of November 17, down $317 million from $14.063 billion as of November 10. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported it spent $125 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the one-week period. As reported, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed last week that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market November 14. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also reported Wednesday that the average interbank lending rate (TIIP) stood at 55.3731%, down 14.3415% from the previous week. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1555GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbn09ea1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
