\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's reserves fall after peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Nov 14 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves fell $97 million to $14.06 billion in the week ended November 10, partly because of $175 million spent in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso, Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Besides the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said reserves were drained by a $170 million payment to the International Monetary Fund and Tesobono amortizations of $103 million. \par \par \uc2  The fall was partly offset by net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases by the government of $212 million, and $139 million netted from \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of state-owned firms such as oil giant Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex). \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the monetary base as of November 10 was 49.176 billion pesos, down from 49.847 billion pesos the previous week. Net domestic credit -- monetary base minus reserves -- stood at a negative 60.795 billion pesos versus a negative 51.358 billion pesos the week before. \par \par \uc2  In its breakdown of the assets side of its balance sheet, it said holdings of government securities fell to 14.38 billion pesos November 10 from 15.10 billion pesos previously. \par \par \uc2  Credits to banks also dropped to 123.09 billion pesos from 126.56 billion. \par \par \uc2  On the liabilities side, Banco de Mexico said its obligations to the IMF last week rose to 113.39 billion pesos from 103.00 billion pesos, and to foreign financial authorities to 11.42 billion pesos from 10.44 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2  Deposits in the current account of the government were 44.26 billion pesos, down from 46.51 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2  Its other debts and share capital were 29.21 billion pesos, versus 33.06 billion pesos in the week ended November 3. \par \par \uc2  Within the monetary base, notes and coins in circulation fell to 49.05 billion pesos from 49.77 billion pesos, while bank deposits in its current account last week were 127 million pesos, up from 74 million pesos. \par \par \uc2  -- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9560 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drbf01vq3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
