\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Weaker; Sinks to New Historic Low \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 1995\par 21:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso closed weaker against the dollar for a third straight session in thin trading Wednesday, sinking to a new historic closing low. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 7.9100 pesos against 7.8100 pesos at Tuesday's close. Spreads narrowed to 7.8600/7.9600 pesos per dollar, compared with 7.7500/7.8700 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said light selling pressures continued amid some skepticism toward the projectory of primary Cetes rates and an unenthusiastic response to the government's 1996 budget proposal presented to Congress Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Still, market players moved cautiously amid speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid low volume if peso-selling pressures picked up too much steam. \par \par \uc2  'Everybody felt the Banco de Mexico would come in if the peso climbed above eight (to the dollar) again today,' said one local trader. 'Overall, the market was pretty quiet today.' \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar opened higher at 8.0500 pesos, but some peso-buying orders quickly surfaced in the first hour of trading. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said they saw no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. They added that some dollar orders on the part of Mexican corporations appeared to ease in later trading. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market late Tuesday, pushing the spot dollar rate down after it had soared as high as 8.1500 pesos in intraday trading. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's drop pushed the peso to a new historic closing low against the dollar. Tuesday's close had represented the previous record closing low. The spot dollar's historic intraday high is 8.2500 pesos, reached November 9. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2009GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbf090j8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
