\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens -3: Moves To 7.9000 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 1995\par 16:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Around 1540 GMT, Banamex quoted the spot dollar trading at a mid rate of 7.9000 pesos on a spread of 7.8500/7.9500. \par \par \uc2  Traders said volume was light, continuing a trend that has been in place for several weeks. \par \par \uc2  Although many analysts said last Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been a judicious move, some market watchers were questioning how often the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before such a strategy becomes counter-productive. \par \par \uc2  ``If \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highlights the fact that it is a very shallow market and it can drastically move (the peso), then it makes some sense,'' said Gray Newman, an economist with James Capel in Mexico City. ``The lesson learned last year, though, is that reserves can disappear very quickly.'' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late Tuesday that international reserves as of November 10 stood at $14.063 billion, down $97 million from $14.160 billion as of November 3. It said it spent $175 million to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the period. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have spent less on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In outlining the government's budget plans Tuesday, Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz reiterated that it remains committed to a free-floating exchange rate regime. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, though, have stressed that they reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on occasion and in a discretionary manner. \par \par \uc2  Some market players were speculating Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept 28-day primary Cetes artificially low at Tuesday's weekly Treasury bill auction. \par \par \uc2  ``The 91-day rate appeared natural, but there are some questions about the 28-day rate,'' said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  Overnight Cetes repurchase agreements on the secondary money market closed Tuesday at 80.50%, despite the fact that the Bank of Mexico issued 2.00 billion pesos of 84-day credits at 67.82% in afternoon trading. \par \par \uc2  The peso lost 0.5% against the dollar Tuesday, after falling 2.8% Monday. It ended Tuesday down 56% against the dollar since December 20, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1544GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbf08zfy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
