\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican Stocks Close Dn 0.6% After Late Sell-Off \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 1995\par 23:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexican stocks closed lower in light volume Tuesday after a late sell-off reversed some earlier gains. \par \par \uc2  According to preliminary official information, the market's key IPC index ended down 12.54 points to 2,241.53 - a drop of 0.6%. At the end of 1994, the IPC stood at 2,375.66. \par \par \uc2  Volume totaled 552.8 million pesos on 60.3 million shares traded. \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed the decline to concerns over the dropping peso and soaring interest rates. As reported, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost 0.5% against the dollar to sink to a historic closing low of 7.8100 pesos per dollar, despite some confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the closing minutes. \par \par \uc2  Secondary money market rates, meanwhile, averaged higher for a sixth straight session Tuesday, ending at 80.50%. Some market players are predicting primary Cetes rates could soar more than 10 percentage points at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly Treasury bill auction later Tuesday. Bellwether 28-day primary Cetes rates already jumped 10.87 percentage points to 54.24% at last week's auction. \par \par \uc2  The IPC hit an intraday high of 2,267.10, 0.6% above Monday's close, around 1735 GMT before selling pressures resurfaced. \par \par \uc2  The early gains came from arbitrage activity as market players sold Mexican ADRs in New York and bought local stocks, according to stock dealers. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market appeared to react little Tuesday to a 1996 budget proposal delivered by Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz to Congress around 1700 GMT. \par \par \uc2  'The market didn't get any major surprises,' said one local trader. 'People are going to take their time looking at the details.' \par \par \uc2  The IPC dropped 2.4% Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2200GMT \par \par \uc2  5047 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbe08zzd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
