\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso -3: Business Cites 'Lack Of Confidence' \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1995\par 22:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Analysts have been hard-pressed to explain the continued bruising of the peso, which many had predicted as recently as six weeks ago could still end the year between 6.50 and 6.75 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In a poll of almost three dozen financial specialists contacted in Mexico by the newspaper Reforma, 63% of those questioned cited a 'lack of confidence' for the peso's recent woes. \par \par \uc2  A poll of 349 Mexico City residents conducted by MORI on November 9 revealed that 78% believed their economic situation will be worse 12 months from now - up from 41% in July. Of those polled, 36% said they were most worried by the 'financial crisis' and 12% said their greatest worry was the 'political crisis.' \par \par \uc2  Some observers said the positive effects of last Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could prove to be short lived. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can help when the objective is known,' said David Malpass, an economist with Bear Stearns in New York. 'At this point it is not clear whether Mexico wants the peso stronger, or to depreciate in line with the inflation rate.' \par \par \uc2  Under such circumstances, he said, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  'has a short impact.' Malpass said Bear Stearns continued to stick to its year-end exchange projection of 6.7500 pesos, but that the figure 'depends completely on \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  answering the purpose behind high interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  Market watchers have speculated for months that the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have differed on Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2125GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbd08yqe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
