\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso -2: Falls 2.8% Vs Dlr From Friday Close \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1995\par 21:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The peso closed 2.8% weaker against the dollar from Friday's close, according to Banamex's quotations. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is down 55% against the dollar since Dec. 20, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they believed Monday's afternoon peso rally came without direct help from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'A lot of people were expecting to see some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, but (the afternoon peso) recovery appeared to be a natural one,' said one local trader. \par \par \uc2  Dealers stressed again Monday that trading levels were very low, making the market highly susceptible to any dollar-buying order. Both Mexican and foreign investors were seeking dollars Monday, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  Traders speculated that some investors wanted to see the details of a 1996 federal budget proposal that will be presented to Congress Tuesday before lending any new support to Mexican financial markets. \par \par \uc2  The most recent peso decline came despite weekend developments that most observers judged to be positive. The finance ministry reported Friday afternoon a September trade surplus of $909 million - up from $708 million in August, and the second-largest surplus posted this year. Mexico registered a $943-million surplus in May. \par \par \uc2  Initial reports from local weekend elections in six states indicated little violence and few charges of voting irregularities. A new round of peace negotiations in the cease-fire southern state of Chiapas between Zapatista rebels and government officials, meanwhile, was expected to resume Monday. \par \par \uc2  The peso has taken some hard hits in the past six weeks. The spot dollar ended September at 6.3850 pesos, and closed October at 7.0650 pesos. The peso lost 2.5% against the dollar last week. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the spot dollar soared to a historic intraday high of 8.2500 pesos last Thursday before some Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the rate back down to 7.5500 pesos at the close. The spot dollar rose as high as 7.7700 pesos in intraday trading Friday, but it ended flat after the peso rallied in the final hours. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said monetary authorities didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, but some traders speculated that there had been some light \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on the final trading day of last week. \par \par \uc2  Despite Thursday's estimated $150-million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a statement late last week reiterating its commitment to a free-floating exchange rate regime. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official added Friday, however, that monetary authorities reserved the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on occasion 'in a discretionary manner.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2025GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbd08yhk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
