\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Sharply Weaker At 7.7700 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1995\par 21:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso closed weaker against the dollar in low volume Monday as selling pressures resurfaced in the wake of last Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed the latest peso sell-off to concern over rising interest rates and the continued absence of entries on the part of foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex had the dollar ending at a mid rate level of 7.7700 pesos against 7.5500 pesos at Friday's close. Spreads were 7.7200/7.8200 pesos per dollar, compared with 7.5000/7.6000 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Banco Inverlat, a smaller bank, had the spot dollar ending at a mid rate of 7.7950 pesos on a spread of 7.7700/7.8200. Some banks had the spot dollar closing as high as 7.6000 pesos Friday. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar soared as high as 7.8850 pesos around 1640 GMT before peso-selling pressures eased in later trading. Traders said they saw no signs of renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'We saw some real demand for dollars in the morning,' said the head trader of a U.S. bank in Mexico City. \par \par \uc2  'With the volatility of the market and the huge spreads, it's very difficult to take positions,' the trader added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said there was heightened concern Monday about soaring interest rates. Bellwether 28-day primary Cetes rates rose 10.87 percentage points to 54.24% last week, and some market watchers are predicting rates could climb as much as 15 percentage points at Tuesday's primary \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction. Secondary money market rates averaged 62.09% Friday before moving above 70% Monday. \par \par \uc2  Higher interest rates typically attract foreign investment funds, but not this time, according to market watchers. \par \par \uc2  'The interest rates are so high that they've completely blown the risk-reward ratio to pieces,' said Mary Slack, a New York-based analyst with MCM \b \highlight22\uc2 CurrencyWatch\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 'Nobody can really say what is a break-even point.' \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the sharp increase in interest rates was fueling new concerns about the future health of the domestic banking sector. Higher rates also will postpone prospects of an economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar's historic closing high was reached November 8, when it ended at 7.8000 pesos. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2007GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbd08yfb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
