\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Intraday Peso -2: Vs 7.80 Historic Closing Low \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1995\par 19:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Around 1810 GMT, the spot dollar continued to be quoted at 7.8500 pesos. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar's historic closing high against the dollar is 7.8000 pesos, reached November 8. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investment funds were keeping their distance despite sharp increases in interest rates. Bellwether 28-day primary Cetes rates rose 10.87 percentage points to 54.24% last Tuesday, and some market watchers are predicting rates could climb as much as 15 percentage points at this week's primary \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction. Secondary money market rates averaged 62.09% Friday, and had moved above 70% Monday. \par \par \uc2  'What's creating concern is that rates are so high, and still there doesn't seem to be a lot of (foreign) interest,' said one local trader. \par \par \uc2  Higher rates will place further strain on the Mexican banking sector and postpone prospects of an economic recovery, analysts have pointed out. \par \par \uc2  Traders speculated that some investors wanted to see the details of a 1996 federal budget proposal that will be presented to Congress Tuesday before lending any new support to Mexican financial markets. \par \par \uc2  Weekend developments, meanwhile, were judged positive by most observers. The finance ministry reported Friday afternoon a September trade surplus of $909 million - up from $708 million in August, and the second-largest surplus posted this year. Mexico registered a $943-million surplus in May. \par \par \uc2  Initial reports from local weekend elections in six states indicated little violence and few charges of voting irregularities. A new round of peace negotiations in the cease-fire southern state of Chiapas between Zapatista rebels and government officials, meanwhile, was expected to resume Monday. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed Friday down 17% against the peso since September 20. The spot dollar ended October at 7.0650 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Despite Thursday's estimated $150-million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a statement late last week reiterating its commitment to a free-floating exchange rate regime. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official added Friday, however, that monetary authorities reserved the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on occasion 'in a discretionary manner.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1812GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbd08y3f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
