\par\par \b \uc2  Peso calms as market awaits goverment's next move. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Michael Stott \par \uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 20:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Nov 10 (Reuter) - Mexico's peso, which sank to record lows Thursday before being rescued by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, was little changed Friday as traders awaited the government's next move. \par \par \uc2  The peso opened slightly weaker at 7.70 to the dollar in the most-watched 48-hour contract but later firmed to 7.58 in quiet trading, two centavos above Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  "The peso is too devalued right now, it is at levels which are excessively low and there has to be a correction," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged Thursday to an all-time low of 8.30 to the dollar, generating panic in the market, before Banco de Mexico, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stepped in to sell around $200 million and buy pesos in a bid to support the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Markets have been worried for some time about whether Mexican policy-makers have a clear strategy for hauling the country out of its worst recession in decades. \par \par \uc2  But their concern came to a head this week when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates a steep 10 percentage points in an effort to prop up the wobbly peso. \par \par \uc2  Markets saw the move as a mistake because it would deepen the recession and pounced hard on the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing it down more than 10 percent in a matter of days. \par \par \uc2  The government did not issue a statement on the peso crisis Friday. \par \par \uc2  President Ernesto Zedillo said on Thursday that "sooner rather than later" financial markets would have to face what he termed the reality of Mexico's imminent economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "Today we know we have succeeded in quickly leveling the trade balance, that we have practically liquidated all short-term debt and that hyperinflation has been avoided," he said in a speech in Merida, the capital of the eastern state of Yucatan. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Friday to sell dollars and buy pesos. \par \par \uc2  But traders pointed to a sharp hike in money market interest rates as a signal that the bank was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  there to make pesos more attractive. \par \par \uc2  Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action on Thursday drew strong criticism from one U.S. senator who has long opposed Washington giving aid to Mexico. \par \par \uc2  Sen. Alfonse D'Amato, a New York Republican, attacked President Zedillo's government for spending "U.S. taxpayer dollars in a frantic and futile attempt to support the peso" -- a reference to the $12.5 billion in loans from the U.S. Treasury to Mexico to help it through its economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  Zedillo said in his Merida speech that Mexico had managed to rebuild its international reserves "which guarantees the solvency of our economy" -- a reference to the fact that the official reserves now stand at $14.16 billion. \par \par \uc2  But private economists and financial market analysts were sceptical. They said the reserves were more than outweighed by the dollars Mexico owes in short-term loans to the United States and the International Monetary Fund (IMF). \par \par \uc2  This means the country effectively has negative reserves and will continue to have trouble defending its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drba021ke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
