\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican peso steadies after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Henry Tricks \par \uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Nov 10 (Reuter) - Relative calm returned to \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso market in the wake of Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded from early lows in thin trade, giving the stock market a boost. \par \par \uc2  Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied market rumors that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give the peso a helping hand Friday morning. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market was still trying to fathom the implications of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in almost six months, and many players were on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  One question concerning analysts was to what extent Banco de Mexico would keep liquidity in check in the money market to put upward pressure on interest rates and bolster its defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said late Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was accompanied by a drain on liquidity in the money market to raise rates. \par \par \uc2  "The problem is interest rates lead to a vicious circle. A rise in rates is mortal for banks and for public finances. I'm very scared about the bank problem," said Rodolfo Navarrete, economist at Vector brokerage in Mexico. \par \par \uc2  Treasury bill, or Cetes, rates continued to soar in same-day trade, amid a push by speculators in the money market to see how high Banco de Mexico was ready to let interest rates go in its efforts to attract peso buyers. \par \par \uc2  Their efforts were rewarded. In its daily liquidity auction the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 42- and six-day credit at 64.81 percent and 67.38 percent, a level that traders said indicated Banco de Mexico would sell benchmark 28-day Cetes above 64 percent in next weeks's primary auction. \par \par \uc2  That's would be a stunning increase of 10 percentage points, hard on the heels of a similar rate hike last week. \par \par \uc2  Investors continue to fret about the impact on Mexico's recession-struck economy of the recent bout of financial market turmoil, worrying that tighter credit will stifle any recovery. \par \par \uc2  Few believe that Banco de Mexico's suprise dollar selling in the markets Thursday is anything but a temporary solution to the peso's woes. \par \par \uc2  Banco de Mexico's reserves are currently in a net negative position, which limits its capacity to dig into its own coffers to sell dollars in support of the peso. \par \par \uc2  Mexico's hands are also tied by a strong anti-Mexican tide of sentiment in the U.S. Congress, that analysts say may prevent Mexico City from borrowing more U.S. money to help bail out the Government. \par \par \uc2  It has already taken $12.5 billion from the U.S. Treasury to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. Before this month's round of peso upheaval, Mexican president Ernesto Zedillo had tactfully said he had no plans to borrow more. \par \par \uc2  In the immediate future, analysts said, the market will be waiting for Tuesday's 1996 budget announcement to see whether Zedillo has any more plans up his sleeve to rescue the country from crisis and restore investors' battered confidence. \par \par \uc2  -- Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9560 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drba021ja\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
