\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican peso seen lulled by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Henry Tricks \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Nov 10 (Reuter) - Peso trading is expected to be relatively quiet at the opening following Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets yesterday to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If the market opens up with people strongly buying dollars we could be off to the races again. But that's not usually the most likely scenario -- people will watch and wait," said Denis Parisien, an analyst at I.D.E.A. in New York, late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since May 14 Thursday, selling what it described as a "modest" amount of dollars when the peso hit a record low of 8.30 against the dollar, helping it rebound to 7.60. \par \par \uc2  A Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  source told Reuters Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was supported by a drain of liquidity in the money market. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Operationally\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this was done by reducing the (cash) balances of banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  He declined to specify whether there would be further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying such a move was discretionary. \par \par \uc2  "The wise element of a free-floating exchange rate is that central bankers always leave themselves the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the source said. \par \par \uc2  Many analysts think the market will test Banco de Mexico again in coming days, pushing the peso down to see how low it can go before there is more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Once you go out in as visible fashion as they did Thursday, people are going to say 'fine, but what about tomorrow'," said Rob Rauch, head of sales and trading at the Weston Group in New York. "It's not something you can do just once." \par \par \uc2  There were unconfirmed rumors in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that Banco de Mexico's move followed or coincided with a large and timely peso order by either a U.S. hedge fund or Mexican and U.S. banks. They would have made a fortune if they bought the peso at its lows. \par \par \uc2  But traders who caught the wrong side of the rebound with short peso positions were badly burned, and Parisien expected them to lick their wounds Friday rather than test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's defensive strength anew. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. Veteran's Day holiday Friday could also cool the market, but several analysts said Banco de Mexico is unlikely to enjoy a lull for long. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the government unveils its budget proposals for 1996, and if they fail to contain strong enough measures to rescue Mexico's economy, many believe the peso could come in for a new battering. \par \par \uc2  Also, Banco de Mexico's reserves are still depleted, despite some $12.5 billion in U.S. support received earlier this year. \par \par \uc2  With Washington embroiled in a battle between the White House and Congress over raising the U.S. debt ceiling, it is not considered a good time for Mexico to be liberally spending what it has left to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Rauch said the government of President Ernesto Zedillo may have a hard time convincing investors that they have any plans up their sleeve to restore order to the economy, because confidence has sunk so low. \par \par \uc2  He said he would like to see a clearer definition from the Finance Ministry and Banco de Mexico on whether their priority was spurring growth or taming inflation. \par \par \uc2  -- Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9560 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drba01y48\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
