\par\par \b \uc2  Banco de  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  statement on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Nov 10 (Reuter) - The following is a Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement issued early Friday on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday: \par \par \uc2  "Late last year the Bank of Mexico adopted a floating exchange rate regime. Since May 14, the Bank has followed a virtually free float, without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  In recent weeks, and in particular over the last few days and in today's session, the peso had shown considerable volatility and depreciated at a fast rate, reaching the level of N$8.30 per $1 U.S. dollar, a behavior unrelated to the fundamentals of the economy. \par \par \uc2  "In light of the above, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Commission, composed by the Secretary and two Undersecretaries of the Treasury and the Governor and two Deputy Governors of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , decided that the Bank should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As a result, the peso strengthened closing at N$7.60 pesos per $1 U.S.. A small amount of reserves was used in this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Comission deemed that this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , wich does not imply the abandonment of a floating exchange rate policy, is appropiate given current budgetary and monetary policies. The 1996 Budget, to be presented to Congress next week, emphasizes the maintenance of solid public finances. \par \par \uc2  "In turn, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the credit markets to reduce the balances of banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  -- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289560 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drba01y47\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
