\par\par \b \uc2  Mixed Reviews On Mexican Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 : Analysts \b0\par\par\uc2  By Matt Smith \par \uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 21:45\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY (DJ-EMR)--Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets has drawn criticism in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the start down a slippery slope of dwindling reserves, but analysts interviewed Friday said the alternative may have been worse. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a dangerous policy," said \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City economist Jonathan Heath. "But in this situation, you don't have too many alternatives." \par \par \uc2  Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets seemed to have stabilized midday Friday, with the dollar closing at at 7.55 pesos, unchanged from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Volatile trading Thursday drove the dollar as high as 8.25 pesos, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in with what analysts estimate was $150 million to $200 million of peso purchases. \par \par \uc2  Traders said it was too early to determine Friday the medium-term effects of Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the relative calm of the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar did move up to 7.77 pesos bfore dropping to below 7.70 pesos, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially denied participating in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday. \par \par \uc2  While the bank officials routinely deny entering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets even when traders say otherwise, on Thursday the authorities made a point of confirming their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader who spoke with Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  participation would have been easy to detect given Friday's thin market. \par \par \uc2  "We haven't seen a thing," the trader said. "Today is turning into essentially a rest day. The whole week was very volatile, and market participants are waiting to see what happens. I think next week is going to be very active." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 11-10-95 \par \par \uc2  1545EST \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011025drba00bmj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
