\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  News: Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Tops Headlines \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 16:39\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY (DJ-EMR)--The following summary is based on Friday editions of the Mexico City dailies Reforma, La Jornada, El Financiero and The News. \par \par \uc2  -- The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday afternoon topped headlines Friday, with Mexican bankers generally praising the move. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it stepped in to halt the continued depreciation of the Mexican peso, spending some $150 million to reverse a low of 8.40 pesos to the dollar, helping the peso recover to a closing level of 7.60 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted in a classic fashion, just as central banks tend to do in this type of situation," a financial director at Banamex, Mexico's largest bank, was quoted in El Financiero as saying. \par \par \uc2  -- Labor and business leaders said they may withdraw from the latest version of the government's anti-inflation "pacto" agreement given the government's inability to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable, a part of the deal, El Financiero reported. \par \par \uc2  The latest pacto drafted last week was billed as the "Alliance for Economic Recuperation," and was a continuation of wage cap agreements successfully used during the administration of former president Carlos Salinas de Gortari to halt inflation. \par \par \uc2  Government officials told El Financiero there was no need to re-negotiate the new pacto, saying that prices hadn't appreciated notably since the peso began to drop in value three weeks ago, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 11-10-95 \par \par \uc2  1039EST \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011025drba00bfi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
