\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico Intraday Peso Trading At 7.60 Vs Dlr; Few Trades \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 19:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso eased from earlier drops against the dollar in cautious intraday trading Friday following Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City a little after 1845 GMT, on spot dollar markets, the dollar was being quoted at mid rate levels of 7.6000 pesos against 7.5500 pesos at Thursday's close. Spreads were 7.5500/7.6500 pesos per dollar, compared with 7.5000/7.6000 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said volume was extremely low, with market players treading cautiously after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the closing minutes of trading Thursday to put the brakes on a sharp peso sell-off. \par \par \uc2  'Everybody figures the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very close to the market, and that it will move quickly if there's any big shift,' said one local trader with a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar moved as high as 7.7700 pesos in the first 90 minutes of trading before it dropped back below 7.7000 pesos shortly afterward. Traders said some Mexican corporations took advantage of Thursday's late peso rally to pick up cheaper dollars for future debt payments. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official dismissed some speculation among traders that the Bank of Mexico may have lent light support to the peso in early trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  'Up until 12 pm (1800 GMT) there has been no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whatsoever,' the official said, adding that the bank reserved the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market 'in a discretionary manner.' \par \par \uc2  As reported, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the final minutes of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading Thursday to halt a major sell-off of pesos that had pushed the spot dollar as high as 8.2500 pesos in intraday trading. The spot dollar was trading around 8.0000 pesos when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred. \par \par \uc2  The peso dived 4.0% against the dollar in very light volume Wednesday to end at a historic closing low of 7.8000 pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1851GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drba08ww0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
