\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico Peso/Amplifier-2: Interest Rates Could Go Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 03:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Michel Camdessus, head of the International Monetary Fund, said Mexico must meet certain targets within certain time periods, but that doesn't prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves do 'not mean at all that there is a change of strategy in the free float (of the peso) or in their relation with the IMF,' Camdessus said, adding that peso speculation is out of hand given Mexico's 'strengthening fundamentals.' \par \par \uc2  In Congress, the peso's fall brought a new attack by critics of the Clinton administration's policy. Senator Alfonse D'Amato, chairman of the Senate Banking Committee, said the 'Mexican government will spend U.S. taxpayer dollars in a frantic and futile effort to support the peso.' \par \par \uc2  In Mexico, a senior Finance Ministry official said the government saw no choice but to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - 23% between Sept. 20 and the start of trading Thursday - had become so debilitating that it was endangering the government's economic program for next year. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry official said the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after a morning meeting among top officials, who noted that an attempt to help the peso by sharply pushing up short-term interest rates failed Tuesday. The official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also was committed to a drastic increase in interbank interest rates if that's what it takes to halt speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders quickly tested Mexican government's resolve Thursday. Bankers here said there was a tense struggle in the trading rooms in the last half-hour of peso trading. 'This is a clear confrontation between the Banco de Mexico and the speculators,' one banker said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-11-95 \par \par \uc2  0258GMT \par \par \uc2  1124 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drba08qtk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
