\par\par \b \uc2  (WSJ):  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  Peso Up As Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 : Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By CRAIG TORRES and PAUL B. CARROLL \par \uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 03:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY (AP-DJ)--The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after seven weeks of standing aside while the peso slid to record lows, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  powerfully in the market Thursday, helping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  close up more than 3% against the dollar, Friday's Wall Street Journal reports. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which caught traders by surprise, rescued the peso from what appeared certain to be its third swoon in as many days. Mexican officials said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about $150 million to buy pesos, dominating a market in which trading had recently been only about $200 million a day. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sellers pushed the peso down 5.5% Thursday to a record intraday low of 8.25 to the dollar. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's buying buoyed the peso to a close of 7.55 to the dollar, up from Wednesday's close of 7.80. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican stock market's IPC index rose 76.62 points, or 3.43%, to 2311.09. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was carried out in close consultation with U.S. authorities, officials said. The U.S. has closely monitored Mexico's economic performance since assembling a $50 billion international loan package to help the country through the crisis caused by last December's sharp peso devaluation. \par \par \uc2  In Washington, a senior Treasury official praised Mexico, saying, 'In the face of volatility, Mexican officials have reemphasized the importance of sticking with their monetary and fiscal policy.' \par \par \uc2  Although many traders had assumed that the international bailout prohibited Mexico from spending its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to bolster the peso, officials involved in the accord said that isn't the case. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-11-95 \par \par \uc2  0255GMT \par \par \uc2  1124 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drba08qt0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
