\par\par \b \uc2  World Stocks -13: U.S. Surges; Canada, Mexico Up \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 00:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK: [5042] \par \par \uc2  Another rally in the volatile technology sector produced a shining session for the stock market, as major indexes climbed to records for the second straight day. A key reading confirmed the perception that the economy's growth has slowed. The Labor Department said the producer price index dipped 0.1% last month amid a continued decline in energy prices. The more important data came out after the market closed yesterday and showed that demand for semiconductors was surprisingly high. Volume reached 379.5 million shares on the NYSE. \par \par \uc2  DJIA: 4,864.95 (prelim) 4,852.67 End 1994: 3834.44 \par \par \uc2  TORONTO: [5046] \par \par \uc2  Shares ended in positive territory for the first time since Monday, but the gains were limited as the market continues to rest following last week's rally. Advances led declines 391 to 363, volume slipped to 62,903,000 shares from 66,805,000 shares and trading value was C$862.9 million vs C$778.8 million. Among gold stocks, Barrick Gold Corp. and Placer Dome Inc. rose 7/8 to 34 5/8 and 5/8 to 32 3/4, repectively. \par \par \uc2  TSE 300: 4,581.96 4,576.35  End 1994: 4213.61 \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY: [5047] \par \par \uc2  Stocks closed higher in heavy trading, as some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange market gave further fuel to bargain-hunting. Volume totaled 967.2 million pesos on 104.2 million shares traded - the most active session since Oct. 5. As reported, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, prompting a sudden rally in the peso in the final minutes of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  IPC: 2,311.09  2,234.47 End 1994: 2375.66 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2334GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drb908wsi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
