\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 /Peso -4: Interest Rates Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 1995\par 23:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Observers said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities apparently wanted to send a strong message to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after a string of peso falls marked by low volume and high speculation. \par \par \uc2  'We saw a very crazy market today,' said one local trader of Thursday's volatility. 'Today was the craziest.' \par \par \uc2  Until Thursday, Mexican monetary authorities had stood resolutely on the sidelines during the recent sharp declines in the peso, which dropped 9.6% in October to end last month at 7.0650 pesos. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  then fell again during the first five trading sessions in November. \par \par \uc2  Initial reactions to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were cautious. \par \par \uc2  'I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was done to modulate a market that is moving in a downward direction,' said Jim Nash, an economist at the Nomura Research Institute in New York. 'How far the market (now) moves depends on government credibility and whether investors believe the downside has been eliminated.' \par \par \uc2  Some observers pointed out that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave the peso a much-needed boost amid a protracted speculative sell-off, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  lacks sufficient international reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on a regular basis. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported Tuesday that its reserves stood at $14.160 billion as of November 3. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also tried to restore some order Thursday through the secondary money market, where it issued 1.44 billion pesos in 14-day credits at a very high 61.72% in late trading. \par \par \uc2  As reported, bellwether 28-day Cetes rates soared 10.87 percentage points to 54.24% at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's primary auction of Treasury bills Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2254GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drb908wox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
