\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican Stocks Close Higher 3.4% On Stronger Peso \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 1995\par 23:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexican stocks closed higher Thursday in heavy trading, as some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange market gave further fuel to bargain-hunting. \par \par \uc2  According to preliminary official information, the market's key IPC index rose 76.72 points to 2,311.09 - a gain of 3.4%. At the end of 1994, the IPC stood at 2,375.66. \par \par \uc2  Volume totaled 967.2 million pesos on 104.2 million shares traded - the most active session since Oct. 5. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, prompting a sudden rally in the peso in the final minutes of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex had the dollar ending at mid rate levels of 7.5500 pesos against 7.8000 pesos at Wednesday's close. The spot dollar had soared as high as 8.2500 pesos in intraday trading. \par \par \uc2  After opening slightly lower in the opening minutes, stocks rebounded on strong advances in shares belonging to Telefonos de Mexico (Telmex). Traders said the market has been ripe for bottom-fishing following recent declines. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that the sudden surge in the peso against the dollar around 1915 GMT propelled the IPC to an intraday high of 2,324.16, up 4.0% from Wednesday's close, at around 1950 GMT. \par \par \uc2  'Stocks were trying to advance all day. When the dollar fell below 8.05 pesos, the stocks began to move higher,' a local trader said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors placed some early buy orders, while domestic investors appeared to be the driving force in the market during later trading, according to observers. \par \par \uc2  'Foreign investors were trading heavier in the morning, but weren't making a strong presence in the afternoon rally ' said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the Bank of Mexico announced that the consumer price index rose 2.06% for the month of October, but the news had little effect on the market. \par \par \uc2  'It seems to have fallen within the market consensus,' said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Consumer prices rose 2.07% in September, after they rose 1.66% in August. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-11-95 \par \par \uc2  2205GMT \par \par \uc2  5047 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drb908whl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
