\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens -4: Moves to 7.2450 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 1995\par 17:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Around 1610 GMT, the spot dollar moved higher to a mid rate of 7.2450 pesos on a spread of 7.2200/7.2700. \par \par \uc2  The peso last closed weaker March 9, when the spot dollar ended at 7.4500 pesos. \par \par \uc2  'There's not a lot of foreigners around, but the few that are, appear to be selling their pesos. We've seen some foreign investors exit,' said one local trader, who characterized overall volume as 'moderate.' \par \par \uc2  A little after 1600 GMT, December futures contracts on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange were trading at 7.6336 pesos per dollar after closing Tuesday at 7.4738 pesos/dlr. \par \par \uc2  The key IPC index on Mexico City's stock exchange was trading at 2,278.45, down 1.0% from Tuesday's close, in light volume. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in Mexico City said there were no signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. In recent days, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  has attempted to lend some support to its beleagured \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by pupshing interest rates higher on the secondary money market. \par \par \uc2  That policy has had a limited effect. \par \par \uc2  'We're not seeing a lot of foreigners bring their funds into the money market,' said one local trader. 'With the high interest rates, you're hearing a lot of new concern about the economy.' \par \par \uc2  The government is predicting its new economic plan will prompt 3% economic growth in 1996 after what is expected to be a 5.5% contraction this year. The longer interest rates stay high, observers say, the more difficult it will be to reach that target. \par \par \uc2  Rudiger Dornbusch, a prominent economics professor at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, argued Tuesday that the Mexican government should let the peso depreciate even further in order to stimulate exports, rather then attempt to lend it support through higher interest rates. Dornbush's name was being referred to quite frequently in early trading Wednesday, according to local dealers. \par \par \uc2  Secondary money market rates Tuesday averaged 45.63%, up 1.09 percentage points from Monday, while bellwether 29-day primary Cetes rates rose 1.14 percentage points to 43.37% at auction Monday - the fifth straight week that primary rates were up across the board. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Mexico's international reserves stood at $13.567 billion on Oct. 27, slightly lower than the $13.660 billion reported as of Oct. 20. International reserves stood at $14.699 billion on Sept. 29. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1610GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drb108k8a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
