\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico News -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  To Stay Out of  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Markets \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 1995\par 18:25\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, bank director Miguel Mancera told El Financiero. The $14.8 billion in international reserves the bank held as of Oct. 6 came mostly from money loaned as part of a U.S./International Monetary Fund bailout. \par \par \uc2  The bailout money is to be used exclusively for paying back money owed on Tesobonos and other short-term debt instruments, according to stipulations included in the loan package. \par \par \uc2  Mancera's statement doesn't necessarily mean the Mexican government will keep its hands out of peso/dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican government has traditionally used several federal entities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, not just the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , economists told Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report. \par \par \uc2  The development bank Nacional Financiera, the export bank Bancomext, and the government-owned petroleum monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos have all been known to buy Mexican pesos when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value has been threatened, said Roberto Salinas, a Mexico City economist. \par \par \uc2  -- Some 60% of Mexican credit unions are near insolvency, El Financiero reported. \par \par \uc2  -- Foreign companies have committed $8 billion to telecommunications projects in Mexico, El Financiero reported. \par \par \uc2  -- Mexican businesses should get tax breaks to help cope with the country's economic crisis, industry chamber leaders told El Financiero. \par \par \uc2  -- Matt Smith \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 10-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1225EDT \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011025drab00avw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
