\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens Slightly Stronger At 6.3750 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1995\par 17:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso opened slightly stronger against the dollar in light volume Friday as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  clawed back for a second straight day from earlier sharp drops. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City a little after 1500 GMT, on spot dollar markets, the dollar opened at mid rate levels of 6.3750 pesos against 6.3850 pesos at Thursday's close. Spreads were 6.3700/6.3800 pesos per dollar, compared with 6.3800/6.3900 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso was being helped by an easing of month's end selling pressures, with a drop off for a second straight day in corporate dollar demand to cover foreign debt payment obligations. \par \par \uc2  Widely reported \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday morning also appeared to put the brakes on some speculative selling of pesos. \par \par \uc2  'It's very peaceful right now, without a lot of volume,' said a local trader. \par \par \uc2  As reported, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said there was wide consensus that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market through major Mexican banks in the first hour of trading Thursday after the dollar opened at 6.4600 pesos. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on rumors. \par \par \uc2  The assumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the peso gain 1.0% on the dollar Thursday, after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dropped against its U.S. counterpart in seven of the previous eight trading sessions. The spot dollar ended Wednesday at 6.4500 pesos, its highest closing level since April 4. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-09-95 \par \par \uc2  1522GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9t07lt8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
