\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican Stocks Rally To Close Up 1.6% After Peso Rebound \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1995\par 22:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexican stocks overcame a shaky start to close higher for the first time in five sessions amid healthy volume Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the key IPC index rallied from its lowest levels in almost three months after a widely reported \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebound from several days of declines. \par \par \uc2  According to preliminary official information, the market's key IPC index ended up 38.43 points to 2,381.49 - a gain of 1.6%. At the end of 1994, the IPC stood at 2,375.66. \par \par \uc2  Volume totaled 1.46 billion pesos on 125.7 million shares traded - the third straight session that volume surpassed 1 billion pesos. Volume has only exceeded 1 billion pesos six times this month. \par \par \uc2  The IPC had dropped to 2,313.75 at 1530 GMT before staging a sharp rebound on the heels of a rally in the peso. There was general consensus among \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market through the state development bank Nafin and probably a couple other major Mexican financial intermediaries during the first hour of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  'The recovery of the peso really helped the stock market, even though it was an artificial one,' said one local stock trader. \par \par \uc2  The peso had fallen in seven of the eight previous trading sessions to end Wednesday at its weakest level since April 4, but it gained 1.0% on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday to close at 6.3850 pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Also helping the local market was a slight rebound in the Dow Jones Industrial Average and a solid performance in Mexican ADRs traded in New York. But traders added that the local market still remains delicate. \par \par \uc2  'I saw some more foreign participation today, but a lot of them were selling,' said a local trader. 'Investors are still concerned about the economy and the political situation.' \par \par \uc2  The IPC lost 214.04 points in the previous four trading sessions amid a heightened sell-off. It ended Wednesday at its lowest level since July 5, when it closed at 2,306.30. The index had reached a 10-month high of 2,622.21 on September 8 before selling pressures set in. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-09-95 \par \par \uc2  2041GMT \par \par \uc2  5047 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9s07jsm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
