\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Stronger At 6.3850 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1995\par 21:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso rebounded sharply to close stronger against the dollar in moderate volume Thursday amid widespread reports that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Traders said an easing of end-of-month selling pressures also helped the peso rally from Wednesday's close, when it ended at its weakest level in more than five months. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 6.3850 pesos against 6.4500 pesos at Wednesday's close. Spreads were 6.3800/6.3900 pesos per dollar, compared with 6.4400/6.4600 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  There was general consensus among traders that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market through the state development bank Nafin and probably a couple other major Mexican financial intermediaries during the first hour of trading. \par \par \uc2  'The peso strengthened very suddenly, and a lot of people think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave it some support through (banking leaders) Banamex and Bancomer,' said one local trader. 'There wasn't any news that would cause such a shift (in the exchange rate).' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The spot dollar opened at a mid rate of 6.4600 pesos before the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  embarked on a sudden rally. \par \par \uc2  Traders added that fewer Mexican companies were buying dollars to cover month's end foreign debt payment obligations. Mexican banks that had been busy covering end-of-quarter postions meanwhile stopped shedding pesos after the apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'There was a lot of pressure yesterday on account of the end of the month and the end of the quarter, but there was a lot less of that today,' said one Mexico City \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  The peso had declined against the dollar in seven of the previous trading sessions to end Wednesday at its weakest closing level since April 4, when it finished at 6.5250 pesos. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar ended August at 6.2600 pesos. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-09-95 \par \par \uc2  1955GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9s07jpg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
