\par\par \b \uc2  ADR Report: Foreign Shares Firmer On Wall Street Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1995\par 23:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones News Service \par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -DJ- Foreign shares ended the session higher on Wall Street gains and a weaker dollar. \par \par \uc2  Markets across Europe fell, but the dollar fell against foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , strengthening the value of foreign shares traded in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was trading at 99.35 yen and 1.4205 Deutsche marks in the spot market, compared with 100.46 yen and 1.4247 marks late yesterday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expect overseas markets to open firmer following Wall Street's modest gains today. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average gained 24.56 to 4,786.91, according to preliminary figures. \par \par \uc2  The market focused on the telecommunications sector, one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Sweden's telecommunications group L.M. Ericsson rallied on the first day of trading excluding rights to participate in the company's 7.8 billion-krona rights issue. Ericsson jumped 1 3/8 to 24 1/2. \par \par \uc2  Following Ericsson's gains, Finland's Nokia added 2 1/4 to 68 1/4. \par \par \uc2  France's Alcatel-Alsthom was one of the session's biggest losers. Shares of the telecommunications giant plunged after yesterday reporting a first-half loss and a charge of more than $2 billion for restructuring. Alcatel shed 3 1/8 to 17 3/8. \par \par \uc2  France's consumer products group Unilever gained on news that Unilever France, a unit of Unilever PLC, acquired a 51% stake in the French soft drinks business Jerome SA, the holding company of Choky SA. Shares of Unilever gained 1 1/2 to 80. \par \par \uc2  Among U.K. shares, Grand Metropolitan PLC slipped after the food and drinks company, responding to rumors roiling its stock, said its Burger King Corp. fast-food chain isn't for sale. Grand Metropolitan eased 1/4 to 27 7/8. \par \par \uc2  Mexican ADRs followed the local market higher as the peso rebounded sharply to close stronger against the dollar in moderate volume amid widespread reports that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at midrate levels of 6.3850 pesos against 6.4500 pesos at yesterday's close. \par \par \uc2  Telmex gained 5/8 to 31 5/8, Grupo Televisa added 3/4 to 19 7/8, and Bufete Industrial shot up 1 1/8 to 17. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 09-28-95 \par \par \uc2  5:18 PM \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020011025dr9s049oc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
