\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso -2: Also Weakens In Chicago Futures \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 1995\par 22:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The spot peso closed 0.2% weaker against the dollar from Tuesday's close, and is down 45% against the dollar since Dec. 20, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  In peso futures trading on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange, December contracts ended at 6.6979 pesos/dollar compared with Tuesday's close of 6.6845 pesos/dlr. March contracts moved to 7.0972 pesos/dlr from 7.0771 pesos/dlr. \par \par \uc2  Traders in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. Several \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said it appeared the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly on Tuesday when the spot dollar reached 6.30 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers said the market was not anticipating another sharp drop in Cetes rates next week, especially amid predictions that September inflation could edge above 2.0% after having fallen to 1.7% in August. \par \par \uc2  'With such a sharp drop in (inflation) rates, a reaction in the peso was automatic,' said one local trader. 'But we could see some equilibrium in rates and the peso in the next few days.' \par \par \uc2  As reported, rates on longer maturities also dropped at Tuesday's primary auction. The rate on 91-day Cetes fell 1.54 percentage points to 33.29%; 181-day Cetes rates dropped 0.61 percentage point to 34.39%; and 364-day paper fell 1.08 percentage points to 34.80%. \par \par \uc2  In other developments, the government said late Tuesday that unemployment reached 7.3% in July, up from 6.6% in June and 3.2% last December. Among the employed, 20% worked less than 35 hours a week during July. In a release, the government attributed the July rise to a seasonal aberration as students entered the labor market during the summer vacation season. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, said late Tuesday international reserves totaled 94.995 billion pesos as of September 15, down slightly from 95.313 billion pesos as of September 8. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-09-95 \par \par \uc2  2008GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9k07bnd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
