\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Slightly Weaker At 6.3000 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 1995\par 21:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso closed slightly lower against the dollar in moderate volume Tuesday as expectations of a drop in Cetes rates pushed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the 6.3000 marker for the first time in three weeks. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 6.3000 pesos against 6.2850 pesos at Monday's close. Spreads were 6.2950/6.3050 pesos per dollar, compared with 6.2800/6.2900 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso was pressured by widening consensus that short-term Cetes rates will drop around 1.0 percentage point at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's primary auction of Treasury bills after markets close Tuesday. Bellwether 28-day Cetes rates edged up 0.10 percentage point at last week's auction to 34.00%, but secondary market rates have moved lower in recent days. \par \par \uc2  There was some market speculation that some light \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have prevented bigger peso losses. That report could not be confirmed, but traders said such an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have taken place indirectly through a foreign bank once the exchange rate touched 6.30 pesos/dollar. \par \par \uc2  'I haven't talked to anyone who can confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but a lot of people think it happened,' said one local trader at a major Mexican bank. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar last finished above 6.30 pesos on August 28, when it ended at 6.3200 pesos. \par \par \uc2  The peso dropped 0.2% against the dollar Monday after having gained 0.2% on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in very light volume last week, when the spot dollar closed no higher than 6.2850 pesos and finished no lower than 6.2700 pesos. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-09-95 \par \par \uc2  1950GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9j079x2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
