\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Weakens To 4-Mth Low Of 6.3700 Per Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1995\par 21:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso closed at its weakest level against the dollar in more than four months Wednesday as cautious Mexican banks continued to buy dollars ahead of President Ernesto Zedillo's September 1 state of the nation address. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 6.3700 pesos against 6.2700 pesos at Tuesday's close. Spreads were 6.3600/6.3800 pesos per dollar, compared with 6.2650/6.2750 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar last finished higher on April 5, when it closed at 6.4350 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Volume was moderate on Wednesday. The same-day dollar mid rate ended at 6.2800 pesos, before 24-hour and 48-hour rates were subjected to increased pressure in later trading. \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed the peso's decline in part to a continued sell-off following last week's reported 10.5% second-quarter decline in the gross domestic product. A lesser contraction had been expected. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers added that Mexican banks were also actively covering long peso positions ahead of Zedillo's address next Friday. \par \par \uc2  'Nobody wants to have any long peso positions right now in case there are surprises in the speech,' said one Mexico City trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders pointed out that the 6.30-mark represents a bellwether of investor confidence. Mexican Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz had predicted in late July that the spot dollar would move between 6.00 and 6.30 pesos during the remainder of 1995. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-08-95 \par \par \uc2  1950GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8n06fwt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
