\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Rebounds To Close At 6.2200 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1995\par 21:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso rebounded sharply from four straight declines to finish stronger against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in moderate volume Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders differed on what prompted the recovery, with some pointing to heightened investor confidence in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  and others suspecting some light \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 6.2200 pesos against 6.2700 pesos at Wednesday's close. Spreads of banking leader Banamex ended at 6.2000/6.2400 pesos per dollar, compared with 6.2500/6.2900 Wednesday. Spreads offered by other banks narrowed to as little as two centavos. \par \par \uc2  Some traders pointed to the narrowing spreads as signalling an upturn in investor confidence, adding that some foreign investment managers entered the market to buy Mexican government paper Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that positive inflation figures for the first half of June could be released as early as Thursday also gave some boost to the peso, they said. Consumer prices rose 4.2% in May after having jumped 8.0% in April. \par \par \uc2  Approval Wednesday by the Inter-American Development Bank of a $1.25 billion loan package to Mexico Wednesday meanwhile may have soothed some investor concerns about the country's ability to meet debt payments. The World Bank was also expected to take up three loans to Mexico on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Growing expectations that the U.S. Fed will lower interest rates in July also helped the peso, they said. \par \par \uc2  But other traders questioned the legitimacy of the rebound one day after the peso sank to its weakest closing level since April 12, and suggested that the Bank of Mexico may have been quietly active in an attempt to settle markets unnerved by recent political developments. \par \par \uc2  'The market didn't make much sense to me today when you consider a lot of people are still worried about the political climate,' said one Mexico City trader, adding it wouldn't have taken much for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to affect the market amid relatively low volume. \par \par \uc2  News Wednesday that Mexico's international reserves had dropped more than $300 million in the space of a week has renewed speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on occasion in recent weeks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and traders say the bank never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-06-95 \par \par \uc2  1957GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6m04o3s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
