\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso -2: Intl Reserves Dip A Bit \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1995\par 22:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement Wednesday that Mexico's international reserves as of June 16 had dipped slightly to $10.336 billion from $10.650 billion June 9 also was seen in a negative light by some investors. \par \par \uc2  A few traders, though, saw something positive in the peso's apparent resistence level below the 6.3000 mark. \par \par \uc2  'As soon as the dollar got close to 6.30, people retreated very quickly,' said one Mexico City trader. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said they saw no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  They added that there appeared to be little reaction to Wednesday's approval of a $1.25 billion loan by the Inter-American Development Bank to help shore up Mexico's banking sector and provide some funds for social programs. The loan had been expected. The World Bank, meanwhile, is scheduled to take up three loans to Mexico on Thursday. Preliminary estimates of the outlay are $1.5 billion. \par \par \uc2  The peso also lost some ground in peso futures trading on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange. September contracts moved to 6.8027 pesos/dollar from 6.7751 pesos/dlr; December deliveries moved to 7.3260 pesos/dlr from 7.2886 pesos/dlr. \par \par \uc2  The spot peso closed 0.3% weaker against the dollar from Tuesday's close, and is down 45% against the dollar since Dec. 20, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar closed at 6.1750 pesos at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-06-95 \par \par \uc2  2007GMT \p