\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Weaker Vs Dlr Ahead Of Cetes \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 1995\par 21:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso closed weaker against the dollar in light volume Tuesday amid concern over falling fixed-income yields and possible political instability. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 6.2500 pesos against 6.2000 pesos at Monday's close. Spreads were 6.2300/6.2700 pesos per dollar, compared with 6.1800/6.2200 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said peso demand slackened ahead of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  primary auction of Cetes. The weekly Treasury bill auction is expected to produce another drop in rates and could send some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players off in search of more attractive yields in other countries. Results are expected a few hours after markets close. \par \par \uc2  As reported, bellwether 28-day Cetes fell 5.24 percentage points at last week's primary auction to 47.00%. Secondary money market rates, meanwhile, dropped for the ninth straight session Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders added there also was some speculative selling of the peso amid concern on the political front. As reported, a Mexico City judge who complained of irregularities in the April 8 government-declared bankruptcy of the city's public bus system was found dead of a gunshot wound Tuesday. It was the third violent death of a public official linked to the case, and the second death since Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Relations among the country's three largest political parties, meanwhile, have chilled notably in recent days. The leading conservative opposition National Action Party on Sunday said it would pull out of multi-party democratic reform talks until a post-electoral dispute in the southern state of Yucatan is resolved. \par \par \uc2  The center-left Party of the Democratic Revolution has in the meantime delivered to judicial authorities what it says is documented proof of wild campaign overspending on the part of the ruling party in last November's gubernatorial elections in Tabasco. \par \par \uc2  'There was some speculative movement today because the market was very nervous,' said one Mexico City trader. \par \par \uc2  A couple traders speculated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  lightly Tuesday to ensure that the peso did not lose even more against the dollar. The spot dollar reached an intraday high of 6.2650 pesos before retreating slightly. \par \par \uc2  Before Tuesday's volatility, the spot dollar had closed in a tight trading band of between 6.1750 pesos and 6.2000 pesos in the previous six trading days. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-06-95 \par \par \uc2  1954GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6k04myx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
