\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Slightly Weaker At 6.2000 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1995\par 21:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso closed one centavo weaker against the dollar in very light volume Monday amid expectations that Cetes yields will drop further at Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  primary auction. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, the dollar ended at mid rate levels of 6.2000 pesos against 6.1900 pesos at Friday's close. Spreads were 6.1800/6.2200 pesos per dollar, compared with 6.1700/6.2100 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said there may have been some light \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure that the peso did not lose more ground ahead of another expected drop in Treasury bill rates. Secondary money market rates edged further down Monday for the ninth straight session. Primary 28-day Cetes dropped 5.24 percentage points to 47.00% last Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'You'd normally expect the peso to lose more ahead of a drop in rates, but it wouldn't take much to prop up (the peso) with these volumes,' said one Mexico City trader. \par \par \uc2  Other traders, though, said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was entering a natural consolidation phase after several months of often volatile swings. \par \par \uc2  'Basically the market is very stable right now, and people don't feel any pressure to move one way or the other,' said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar rate ended May at 6.1850 pesos, and closing mid rate quotes last week ranged between a very narrow band of 6.1750 pesos and 6.1900 pesos. \par \par \uc2  In what helped the peso remain stable Monday, Mexican banking leader Banamex was reported to have sold $90 million in dollars on the stock exchange floor's spot dollar market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-06-95 \par \par \uc2  1951GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6j04kc2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
