\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Weaker At 5.8950 Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 1995\par 21:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso closed weaker against the dollar in healthy volume and volatile activity Thursday as some foreign investors took their money out of the local stock market and Mexican companies bought dollars to cover end-of-month foreign payment obligations. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City, on spot dollar markets, the peso rebounded somewhat from a sharp intraday drop to end at mid rate levels of 5.8950 pesos per dollar against 5.7950 pesos per dollar at Wednesday's close. Spreads were 5.8700/5.9200 pesos per dollar, compared with 5.7700/5.8200 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar soared to an intraday high of 6.2350 pesos/dlr around 1800 GMT before the peso recovered some of its loss in the final hour of trading. \par \par \uc2  While a few traders thought there may have been some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most said they believed the market adjusted on its own to finish below the psychological trading level of 6 pesos to the dollar. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The peso performed better on cash dollar markets, ending at 5.7950 pesos/dlr. The 24-hour rate, meanwhile, ended at 5.8650 pesos/dlr. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was an added pressure among some Mexican companies to buy dollars for end-of-month payment obligations ahead of a Mexican long weekend. Local financial markets will be closed Monday for an official holiday, meaning 48-hour spot contracts will be tied up until Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some foreigners who had entered the Mexican Stock Exchange earlier this week were taking their money out and converting it back into dollars ahead of the weekend. A little after 1945 GMT the market's key IPC index was trading at 1,988.91, down 0.9% from Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  A weakening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on peso future contracts traded at the Chicago Mercantile Exchange also caused some nervousness and strong speculative moves on the part of Mexican banks, they added. \par \par \uc2  Secondary money market rates also have dropped in recent days to around 70% after having traded above 80% all of last week, making fixed income investments slightly less attractive for foreigners. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-04-95 \par \par \uc2  1954GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4r031et\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
