\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican new peso under less pressure - officials. \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, March 23 (Reuter) - Speculative attacks on the Mexican new peso have been diminishing in recent days, and Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up has been in very small amounts, a senior Mexican treasury official said. \par \par \uc2  Alejandro Valenzuela, undersecretary for international affairs at the finance ministry, said the failure of the new peso to reach a government target of 6.0 per dollar is something that would be resolved over time as confidence in the government's economic programme strengthens. \par \par \uc2  The peso "without doubt is very undervalued," Valenzuela told a news conference, adding that its weakness in recent days has been in very thin trading. \par \par \uc2  Alejandro Reynoso, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, told the same news conference that interest rates needed to remain high to attract savings, despite the burden this placed on domestic industry. \par \par \uc2  "High interest rates are necessary to maintain domestic savings," he said, adding that a government programme to create inflation-indexed investment units would go some way towards easing the pressure on companies. \par \par \uc2  The officials said there were positive signs that the country is beginning to overcome the worst effects of the December 20 devaluation of the new peso, noting that the trade balance is now positive and that the economy registered a public primary surplus in January. \par \par \uc2  They said that this helped explain why the TIIP interbank interest rate fell more than 18 percentage points to about 91 percent this week. \par \par \uc2  The officials also said that the amount of dollar-denominated Tesobonos in circulation has been reduced to $16.593 billion as of Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the International Monetary Fund was dragging its feet on paying out the balance of a $17.8 billion loan promised to Mexico, Valenzuela of the finance ministry said $10 billion would be made available beginning in April. Mexico has already received $7.8 billion on that loan. \par \par \uc2  -- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9560 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr3n099d0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
