\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico same-day peso closes sharply weaker. \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, March 16 (Reuter) - Mexico's same-day new peso closed sharply weaker but off session lows as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market to defend the peso and speculators took profits from their earlier attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The same-day new peso closed 48 centavos weaker at 7.12/7.22 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There is no news. The peso's fall in the morning was from speculation and it pared losses because of a 'dark hand,'" said one trader, referring to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There was also some profit-taking by speculators," he added. \par \par \uc2  Despite the peso's small show of strength at the end of same-day trade, traders said the peso would continue to come under pressure in ongoing futures trade because the market continues to doubt the peso's fundamental strength. \par \par \uc2  "The peso will probably get weaker. When there is a sinking ship, people don't want to drown," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The 24-hour new peso was 24 centavos weaker at 7.12/7.24 per dollar in ongoing trade. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3g007ia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
