\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Stays Above 7 To Dlr In Intraday Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 17:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-DJ)--Mexico's peso continued to perform weaker against the dollar Thursday in mid-morning trading. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City around 1645 GMT, on the spot dollar market, the dollar was trading at mid rate levels of 7.2700 pesos per dollar against 6.9500 pesos per dollar at Wednesday's close. Spreads were 7.2200/7.3200 pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peso opened at a mid rate of 6.9550 pesos/dlr Thursday and then began a steep decline that hit a mid rate of 7.4500 new pesos/dlr around 1530 GMT before recovering somewhat. \par \par \uc2  Traders were mixed on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prompt the rebound, and officials at the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated they will not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz said earlier this week monetary authorities will allow the peso to continue floating, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  from time to time in an effort to bring stability to the beleagured \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Trading was light and speculative, added dealers. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1649GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3g01z57\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
